Dear author,

I've raised this issue on github. The current munge.R script will throw an error if the columns are not named in the ones mentioned in the code, for example if the effect column was named as "z". It will be a pain if you have dozens of such files whose names are not in the ones listed. It can be more robust by converting all columns names to upper or lower cases, such as by using the below in stead in line 28:
hold_names <- toupper(names(files[[i]])

If you decide to do so, obviously lines 32, 37, 42, 47, and 52 need to be updated as well.

Regards,

patrick

