Dear Veera,

As Michel says, your code would be helpful. We will also want to make certain that you are using the exact same Cognitive Performance and EA same sumstats that were used to derive the cog and noncog sumstats that you are comparing your results to. In the supplement of the biorxiv version of the Demange et al. paper, we indeed report a genetic correlation of 1.0 between the Cognitive Performance variable itself and the Cog factor from the Cholesky. We also report the same heritability and SE for both. Here is the most relevant section:

"We defined our genomic structural equation model such that the latent variable Cog is equivalent to the Cognitive Performance variable. We therefore expected our Cog GWAS to parallel the original Cognitive Performance GWAS. We confirm that both GWAS are highly correlated with a LDSC genetic correlation of 1 (p=.00). Both have a similar SNP heritability: Cog SNP-h2= .1921 (SE=.0061) and CP SNP-h2=.192 (SE=.0062). "

Let's definitely start with the code and go from there.

All the best,

Elliot

